3.3 **Version numbering scheme.** Version numbers are assigned in two parts: a whole number and a decimal. The whole number is incremented when the Board approves a substantive change to the text—for example, a new chapter, a reorganisation of material, or a change to a standing rule that affects more than one department. The decimal is incremented for minor corrections, clarifications, and typographical fixes that do not alter the substance of a rule.

3.4 **Examples of version changes.**

3.5 **Approval of version changes.** No change to the manual, however minor, may be made without the written approval of the Editorial Review Board. The Board shall record its approval in the minutes of its monthly meeting. Changes proposed between meetings may be approved by electronic vote, provided that the vote is unanimous and that the change is reported at the next meeting.

3.6 **Recording of changes.** The Production Coordinator shall maintain a revision log, in the form set out in Appendix C. The log shall record, for each change:

- the version number before and after the change;
- the date of approval;
- the name of the Board member who proposed the change;
- a brief description of the change;
- the section or sections affected.

3.7 **Distribution of updated versions.** When a new version is approved, the Production Coordinator shall:

- send a copy of the updated manual to all department heads within five working days;
- post a notice of the change on the shared drive, in the folder named `ALMANAC_MANUAL`, under the sub-folder `VERSIONS`;
- update the cover page of the manual to show the new version number and the date of approval.

