3.8 **Determining the current version.** Staff who are unsure which version of the manual is current shall consult the cover page of the master copy on the shared drive. The master copy is the only authoritative copy. Personal copies, printed copies, and copies held on individual computers are not authoritative, and may be out of date.

3.9 **Use of superseded versions.** Superseded versions of the manual are retained for reference only, in the sub-folder `VERSIONS\ARCHIVE`. They are not to be used for production work. A rule that appears in a superseded version but not in the current version is not in force.

3.10 **Conflict with the current version.** If a staff member finds that an instruction in a superseded version, or in any other document, conflicts with the current version of this manual, the current version governs. This rule applies even where the conflicting instruction is more recent in date, unless the conflicting instruction is itself a later version of this manual approved by the Board.

