3.13 **Handling of handwritten annotations.** The Board is aware that some staff have, over the years, written notes in the margins of printed copies of earlier instructions. Such annotations are not part of the manual. Where an annotation conflicts with the current version, the annotation is void. Where an annotation is consistent with the current version, it may be treated as a helpful gloss, but it has no authority.

